# In-game reload (Bedrock MCP)

After pack/script/content edits that need a world refresh: finish all edits first, wait for watch if needed (`build-watch.mdc`), then reload **once at the end of your turn** — not after every file, not mid-work.

1. If the world is connected via Bedrock MCP (`user-minecraft-bedrock`): run `/reload all` (`execute_command`), then `send_message` a short status (e.g. `reload done` / `релоад сделан`). Mention reload briefly in the reply to the user. Do not wait for the user to ask.
2. If MCP/world is **not** connected (`needsAuth`, unavailable, or clearly offline): ask the user to connect and always paste the command so they can copy it:
    ```
    /connect localhost:8001/ws
    ```
    (Disconnect: `/connect off`. Same as `docs/game-commands.md`.) Do not only say "not connected". Do not send a fake "reload done" chat.
